  "text": "And the memory wall is only half the story. In a Transformer, every new token attends to every token before it. If the GPU had to recompute all earlier tokens from scratch at each step, generation would collapse. Instead, servers store every past token's Key and Value vectors in VRAM, creating the KV cache.",
